    <string name="faq_a_auto_backup_files">They are currently located in the Android/data folder, which, unfortunately, is inaccessible to some because of the current android policy</string>
    <string name="faq_a_delete_note">Long-press a note on your home screen to see the available options. You may also discover other hidden features as well such as the swipe to edit/preview note.</string>
    <string name="faq_a_developer">WriteOn was created by @3zpnix, an electronic engineering university student who creates small open-source apps and games. This build is maintained by @Brandontake, a vibecoding beginner who forked it and improved it for their own needs.</string>
    <string name="faq_a_feature_requests">Of course! Any feedback or suggestions for improvement are welcome. The developer usually replies within a day or two.</string>
    <string name="faq_a_lost_data">Often times this happens due to some changes within that involves handling the notes database. To restore it back, use the outdated recovery feature from the previous versions of the app.</string>
    <string name="faq_a_open_source">Yes! You may fork it, modify codes to your liking. There\'s nothing shady—no virus, no forced ads—just a clean, open-source app.</string>
    <string name="faq_a_recover_deleted">Yes, you can now restore them from your recycle bin found in your navigation drawer or quick action menu.</string>
    <string name="faq_a_report_issue">You can visit the official GitHub page or come chat with the Developer on his social media account(s).</string>
    <string name="faq_a_update_frequency">The developer usually releases updates every one to two months, depending on how busy the developer is with real life and stuff.</string>
    <string name="faq_a_what_is_writeon">WriteOn is a simple app for taking notes—nothing special. You can add images and many more.</string>
